<div class="boxed">
<table class="imgtable"><tr><td align="left"><p><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.01799"><b>Tree-Guided Identify-Then-Exploit: A Unified Framework of Best Arm Identification and Regret Minimization for Dueling Bandits</b></a>
<br />
<b>Pu Wang</b>, Yao-Xiang Ding
<br />
<i>Preprint: </i> <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.01799">arXiv:2606.01799</a>
<br />
tl;dr: We propose Tree-Guided Identify-Then-Exploit (TG-ITE), the first unified framework for N-armed dueling bandits that jointly handles best arm identification (BAI), weak regret, and strong regret under only the Condorcet-winner assumption. A shared identification primitive, TreeAscent, exploits a tree-based tournament decomposition to locate the Condorcet winner, paired with objective-specific exploitation strategies that achieve bounds closely matching the state of the art.</p>
</td></tr></table>
